      contains the sources used to ground the generated content.
      a	␀␀Output only. The average log probability of the tokens in this candidate. This is a length-normalized score that can be used to compare the quality of candidates of different lengths. A higher average log probability suggests a more confident and coherent response.zÆOutput only. The 0-based index of this candidate in the list of generated responses. This is useful for distinguishing between multiple candidates when `candidate_count` > 1.z¬Output only. The detailed log probability information for the tokens in this candidate. This is useful for debugging, understanding model uncertainty, and identifying potential "hallucinations".zpOutput only. A list of ratings for the safety of a response candidate. There is at most one rating per category.zvOutput only. Metadata returned when the model uses the `url_context` tool to get information from a user-provided URL.z¿Output only. An optional opaque continuation token returned when `finish_reason` is `CONTINUATION`. Clients can pass this token in a subsequent `GenerateContentRequest` to continue generation.c␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀Ûz␀␀<Ä␀V␀^8Ñ␀␀d␀␀␀Qh/␀S[␀S[,␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀;R&␀␀␀S[␀S[,␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀;R&␀␀␀S[␀S[,␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀;R&␀␀␀S[␀S[,␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀;R&␀␀␀S[␀S[,␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀;R&␀␀␀S[␀S[,␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀;R&␀␀␀S[␀S[,␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀;R&␀␀␀S[␀S[,␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀;R&␀␀␀S[␀S[,␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀;R	&␀␀␀S[␀S[	S[
