      model version is uploaded or trained under an existing model ID. The
      version ID is an auto-incrementing decimal number in string
      representation.zãList of deployed models created from this base model. Note that a
      model could have been deployed to endpoints in different locations.z:Labels with user-defined metadata to organize your models.z6Information about the tuned model from the base model.z=The maximum number of input tokens that the model can handle.z@The maximum number of output tokens that the model can generate.z0List of actions that are supported by the model.z4The default checkpoint id of a model version.
      zThe checkpoints of the model.z~Temperature value used for sampling set when the dataset was saved.
      This value is used to tune the degree of randomness.zäThe maximum temperature value used for sampling set when the
      dataset was saved. This value is used to tune the degree of randomness.a…␀␀Optional. Specifies the nucleus sampling threshold. The model
      considers only the smallest set of tokens whose cumulative probability is
      at least `top_p`. This helps generate more diverse and less repetitive
      responses. For example, a `top_p` of 0.9 means the model considers tokens
      until the cumulative probability of the tokens to select from reaches 0.9.
      It's recommended to adjust either temperature or `top_p`, but not both.aA␀␀Optional. Specifies the top-k sampling threshold. The model
      considers only the top k most probable tokens for the next token. This can
      be useful for generating more coherent and less random text. For example,
      a `top_k` of 40 means the model will choose the next word from the 40 most
