⁄GoogleRpcStatusi7␀␀·⁄␀␀The `Status` type defines a logical error model that is suitable for different programming environments, including REST APIs and RPC APIs.

It is used by [gRPC](https://github.com/grpc). Each `Status` message contains
three pieces of data: error code, error message, and error details. You can
find out more about this error model and how to work with it in the [API
Design Guide](https://cloud.google.com/apis/design/errors). This data type is
not supported in Gemini API.
