␀␀rè␀␀zÄOutput only. Identifier. Resource name of a TuningJob. Format: `projects/{project}/locations/{location}/tuningJobs/{tuning_job}`z+Output only. The detailed state of the job.z1Output only. Time when the TuningJob was created.z^Output only. Time when the TuningJob for the first time entered the `JOB_STATE_RUNNING` state.z£Output only. Time when the TuningJob entered any of the following JobStates: `JOB_STATE_SUCCEEDED`, `JOB_STATE_FAILED`, `JOB_STATE_CANCELLED`, `JOB_STATE_EXPIRED`.z?Output only. Time when the TuningJob was most recently updated.z\Output only. Only populated when job's state is `JOB_STATE_FAILED` or `JOB_STATE_CANCELLED`.z+Optional. The description of the TuningJob.zöThe base model that is being tuned. See [Supported models](https://cloud.google.com/vertex-ai/generative-ai/docs/model-reference/tuning#supported_models).zFOutput only. The tuned model resources associated with this TuningJob.z*The pre-tuned model for continuous tuning.z'Tuning Spec for Supervised Fine Tuning.z(Tuning Spec for Preference Optimization.zTuning Spec for Distillation.z%Tuning Spec for Reinforcement Tuning.zGOutput only. The tuning data statistics associated with this TuningJob.z®Customer-managed encryption key options for a TuningJob. If this is set, then all resources created by the TuningJob will be encrypted with the provided encryption key.z<Tuning Spec for open sourced and third party Partner models.˙%Evaluation config for the tuning job.a°␀␀Optional. The user-provided path to custom model weights. Set this field to tune a custom model. The path must be a Cloud Storage directory that contains the model weights in .safetensors format along with associated model metadata files. If this field is set, the base_model field must still be set to indicate which base model the custom model is derived from. This feature is only available for open source models.z0Output only. Evaluation runs for the Tuning Job.z;Output only. The Experiment associated with this TuningJob.z!Tuning Spec for Full Fine Tuning.·Ü␀␀Optional. The labels with user-defined metadata to organize TuningJob and generated resources such as Model and Endpoint. Label keys and values can be no longer than 64 characters (Unicode codepoints), can only contain lowercase letters, numeric characters, underscores and dashes. International characters are allowed. See https://goo.gl/xmQnxf for more information and examples of labels.zòOptional. Cloud Storage path to the directory where tuning job outputs are written to. This field is only available and required for open source models.züOutput only. The resource name of the PipelineJob associated with the TuningJob. Format: `projects/{project}/locations/{location}/pipelineJobs/{pipeline_job}`.a_␀␀The service account that the tuningJob workload runs as. If not specified, the Vertex AI Secure Fine-Tuned Service Agent in the project will be used. See https://cloud.google.com/iam/docs/service-agents#vertex-ai-secure-fine-tuning-service-agent Users starting the pipeline must have the `iam.serviceAccounts.actAs` permission on this service account.aV␀␀Optional. The display name of the TunedModel. The name can be up to 128 characters long and can consist of any UTF-8 characters. For continuous tuning, tuned_model_display_name will by default use the same display name as the pre-tuned model. If a new display name is provided, the tuning job will create a new model instead of a new version.zZOutput only. The detail state of the tuning job (while the overall `JobState` is running).zTuning Spec for Veo Tuning.z!Output only. Tuning Job metadata.z Tuning Spec for Veo LoRA Tuning.r|␀␀zJOutput only. The Cloud Storage metrics URI associated with this TuningJob.c␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀Û ␀␀␀<Ä␀V␀^8Ñ␀␀d␀␀␀QhRS[␀/#␀r$␀␀␀r'␀␀␀)r)␀␀␀rò␀␀s␀␀␀"Är*␀␀␀r+␀␀␀⁄TuningJob.__annotate__`>␀␀s␀␀␀¯Ä␀˜␀*Ò␀*ôÒ␀*r,␀␀␀c␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀Û(␀␀␀Ä␀V␀P␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀\␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀9␀␀␀#␀)z!Whether the tuning job has ended.)rÃ␀␀⁄JOB_STATES_END