Content is generated as quickly as possible, and not in real time. Clients
may choose to buffer and play it out in real time.
Nz[The content that the model has generated as part of the current conversation with the user.rè␀␀z“If true, indicates that the model is done generating. Generation will only start in response to additional client messages. Can be set alongside `content`, indicating that the `content` is the last in the turn.z√If true, indicates that a client message has interrupted current model generation. If the client is playing out the content in realtime, this is a good signal to stop and empty the current queue.r«	␀␀a$␀␀If true, indicates that the model is done generating. When model is
      interrupted while generating there will be no generation_complete message
      in interrupted turn, it will go through interrupted > turn_complete.
      When model assumes realtime playback there will be delay between
      generation_complete and turn_complete that is caused by model
      waiting for playback to finish. If true, indicates that the model
      has finished generating all content. This is a signal to the client
      that it can stop sending messages.u•␀␀␀Input transcription. The transcription is independent to the model
      turn which means it doesn‚Äôt imply any ordering between transcription and
      model turn.u≠␀␀␀Output transcription. The transcription is independent to the model
      turn which means it doesn‚Äôt imply any ordering between transcription and
      model turn.
      z/Metadata related to url context retrieval tool.z Reason for the turn is complete.z±If true, indicates that the model is not generating content because
      it is waiting for more input from the user, e.g. because it expects the
      user to continue talking.z=Low latency transcription updated while the user is speaking.zWThe current activity status of the live session. Always sent alongside `turn_complete`.c␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀Ûj␀␀<Ä␀V␀^8Ñ␀␀d␀␀␀Qh/␀S[␀S[,␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀;R&␀␀␀S[␀S[,␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀;R&␀␀␀S[␀S[,␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀;R&␀␀␀S[␀S[,␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀;R&␀␀␀S[␀S[,␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀;R&␀␀␀S[␀S[,␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀;R&␀␀␀S[␀S[,␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀;R&␀␀␀S[␀S[,␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀;R&␀␀␀S[␀S[,␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀;R	&␀␀␀S[␀S[,␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀␀;R
